Backport of DoS / prototype-pollution mitigation for React Flight (React Server
Components) into next 14.2.25's vendored react-server-dom-* compiled bundles.

CVE-2026-23864 / GHSA-h25m-26qc-wcjf (follow-up to the incomplete fix for
CVE-2025-55184). A crafted HTTP request to an App Router Server Function
endpoint is deserialized by react-server-dom-*'s Flight Reply parser. The
asynchronous model resolver (createModelResolver) writes resolved values back
into the parent object with an attacker-controlled key via a bracket
assignment (parentObject[key] = value). Unlike JSON.parse, this [[Set]] does
not skip the "__proto__" key, allowing prototype pollution / excessive
resource consumption during deserialization.

Upstream root-cause fix: facebook/react de58cca00cf0143259250460017404d4a9598a09
("Add more DoS mitigations to React Flight Reply, and harden React Flight"),
synced into Next.js via vercel/next.js 99b450109dfd12eb5fe3e671e4b480a0cde9bd49
("Sync DoS mitigations for React Flight"), first released in next 15.0.8.

No discrete 14.x upstream fix exists (fix lives entirely in the compiled,
vendored bundles). This patch hand-crafts the upstream `key !== '__proto__'`
guard into the equivalent resolver sink across every loadable server bundle
